# Claude Code Global Guidance

@~/.codex/AGENTS.md

## Claude Code Specific Notes

This file imports the shared, agent-neutral global guidance above (Claude Code
reads `CLAUDE.md`, not `AGENTS.md`) and owns only Claude-Code-specific harness
behaviour. Each mechanic below lives here and nowhere else.

- **Skill syntax.** When a command or workflow mentions a Spellguard setup/reset
  skill, use Claude Code slash syntax: `/spellguard-setup`, `/spellguard-reset`.
- **Edit needs Read.** The Edit tool rejects a file as "not read yet" even if you
  just viewed it via `cat`, `sed`, or `git show`. Use the Read tool first.
- **Long waits.** Avoid blocked `sleep N && <cmd>` chains. Use the Monitor tool's
  until-loop, or a bounded background watcher writing progress to a file you
  re-read.
- **`cd` persistence.** A `cd` to a path *inside* the project persists into later
  Bash calls; a `cd` outside it is reset back to the project root (verified
  2026-07-09). Use absolute paths or an explicit working directory anyway — a
  stray `cd` in one call silently changes where later relative paths resolve.
- **Imports cost context.** `@path/to/file` imports are expanded at session
  launch and still count as context. They are for parity and maintainability,
  not context reduction.
